module bound_call.pos_3

// A BOUND NAMING A PROTOCOL OF STD, MET BY A GENERIC METHOD OF STD: `Vec[T]
// @append[S AsSlice[T]]` takes another vector, and `Vec[T] @ptr()` / `@len()`
// meet the contract only through the substitution the receiver fixes (T :=
// int). Until std's protocols entered the registry (task #14) no such bound
// was judged at all; the first judging compared the receiver literally and
// refused seven files of novac's own source -- this cell is that class.
fn main() {
    mut a = []int.of(1, 2, 3)
    ro b = []int.of(4, 5)
    a.append(b)
    println(a.len())
    println(a[4])
}
